  "question_stem": "The diagram shows a velocity-time graph which models the motion of a car. The graph consists of six straight line segments. The car accelerates from rest to a speed of $20 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ over a period of $5 \\text{ s}$, and then travels at this speed for a further $20 \\text{ s}$. The car then decelerates to a speed of $6 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ over a period of $5 \\text{ s}$. This speed is maintained for a further $(T - 30) \\text{ s}$. The car then accelerates again to a speed of $20 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ over a period of $(50 - T) \\text{ s}$, before decelerating to rest over a period of $10 \\text{ s}$.",
